flowchart LR
    accTitle: The knowledge layer
    accDescr: Each question has one place to answer it. CLAUDE.md holds the rules, MEMORY.md the dated state, the ADRs what binds now and decisions.md what happened when; tickets' frontmatter generates the board and the public wiki, so they cannot drift. Agent auto-memory lives outside the repo.
    %% Sources: CLAUDE.md "Read order", sections 8 (improvement loop), 12 (vault layer) and 13 (docs
    %% layer, the commit hook); memory/MEMORY.md header; docs/working-with-agents.md;
    %% tools/obsidian_sync.py, tools/pending_wiki.py, tools/decision_debt.py.

    subgraph repo["In the repo"]
        claudemd["CLAUDE.md<br/>the rules"]
        memorymd["memory/MEMORY.md<br/>the state, every line dated"]
        adrs["docs/adr<br/>what binds now"]
        decisions["memory/library/decisions.md<br/>what happened, when"]
        lessons["memory/library/lessons.md<br/>mistakes, until they become rules"]
        agentdefs[".claude/agents + TEAM.md<br/>roles, no stale facts"]
        tickets["Tickets: .scratch maps<br/>status in YAML frontmatter"]
        sync["obsidian_sync.py + pending_wiki.py<br/>run by the commit hook"]
        board["vault/Board.md, canvases<br/>ADR index"]
        wiki["docs/index.html<br/>the public wiki"]
    end

    outside["Agent auto-memory<br/>outside the repo"]
    agent("An agent starting work")

    tickets --> sync
    sync --> board
    sync --> wiki
    lessons -->|"graduates into"| claudemd
    lessons -->|"graduates into"| agentdefs
    decisions -->|"standing ones become"| adrs
    agent -->|"1 state"| memorymd
    agent -->|"2 rules"| claudemd
    agent -->|"3 how it fits"| adrs
    agent -->|"what is planned"| board
    agent -.-> outside
